{% extends 'wrapper.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Statement of Principles | {{ parent() }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
    <h2 class="text-center">Statement of Principles of MVforPalestine</h2>
    <p class="text-center"><em>Adopted by vote of the membership on November 17, 2026.</em></p>

    <p>MVforPalestine is organized around the following core commitments:</p>
    <ol>
        <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Palestinian freedom.</strong> We support freedom, self-determination, equal rights, and justice for the
            Palestinian people, and the right of return for refugees and their descendants.
        </li>
        <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Stop the genocide.</strong> We oppose Israel’s US-supported genocidal war on Gaza, ethnic cleansing in the
            West Bank, and all Israeli military aggression. We call for a genuine, immediate and permanent
            ceasefire, an end to the siege, and unimpeded humanitarian access.
        </li>
        <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Anti-Zionism and the weaponization of antisemitism.</strong> We are unconditionally anti-Zionist. We
            oppose Zionism as a supremacist ideology. We reject the false conflation of anti-Zionism and
            criticism of Israel with antisemitism.
        </li>
        <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>No impunity for war criminals.</strong> We support the arrest and prosecution of the war criminals
            responsible for crimes against humanity. These include Benjamin Netanyahu, Itamar Ben-Gvir, and
            others.
        </li>
        <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Reconstruction and reparations.</strong> Israel, which carried out the destruction of Gaza, and the states
            that financed or supplied weapons for that destruction, should pay for the reconstruction of Gaza and
            pay reparations to the surviving Palestinians.
        </li>
        <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>No U.S. military aid to Israel.</strong> We oppose all military aid to Israel. We condemn successive US
            administrations for providing military, political and diplomatic support for Israel.
        </li>
        <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Solidarity with BDS.</strong> We are in solidarity with the Boycott, Divestment and Sanctions movement
            (BDS).
        </li>
        <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Nonviolence and free speech.</strong> Our activities and our speech are nonviolent, lawful, and
            constitutionally protected.
        </li>
    </ol>
{% endblock %}
